{"id":"twitter:2000677578189812066","tweet_id":"2000677578189812066","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2000677578189812066","title":"@silentovercast Also get show how easy it is to create the slop. The citations ended up tilting one way, based on one follow up prompt. Keeping that e","summary":"@silentovercast Also get show how easy it is to create the slop. The citations ended up tilting one way, based on one follow up prompt. Keeping that example to show them an \"over-correction,\" caused by ill-defined prompts And show you don't really \"edit\" a document but recreate it, each time","date":"2025-12-15","published":"2025-12-15T21:21:20+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2000676157520331132","reply_tweet_id":"2000676157520331132","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@silentovercast Also get show how easy it is to create the slop. The citations ended up tilting one way, based on one follow up prompt.<br><br>Keeping that example to show them an &quot;over-correction,&quot; caused by ill-defined prompts<br><br>And show you don&#x27;t really &quot;edit&quot; a document but recreate it, each time</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2000677578189812066","display_date":"December 15, 2025 · 21:21 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
