{"id":"twitter:2000359938011664599","tweet_id":"2000359938011664599","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2000359938011664599","title":"@BobScheurle @BobbyMacslittle @DavidCornDC That's not an FBI quote, but from the DOJs National Institute of Justice. It did support idea assault weapo","summary":"@BobScheurle @BobbyMacslittle @DavidCornDC That's not an FBI quote, but from the DOJs National Institute of Justice. It did support idea assault weapons are used in crimew, but also concluded lethality of Assault Weapons couldn't be determined because of high capacity magazines which had larger impact","date":"2025-12-15","published":"2025-12-15T00:19:08+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/BobScheurle/status/2000341549969011025","reply_tweet_id":"2000341549969011025","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@BobScheurle @BobbyMacslittle @DavidCornDC That&#x27;s not an FBI quote, but from the DOJs National Institute of Justice.<br><br>It did support idea assault weapons are used in crimew, but also concluded lethality of Assault Weapons couldn&#x27;t be determined because of high capacity magazines which had larger impact</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2000359938011664599","display_date":"December 15, 2025 · 00:19 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:2000351369010807090","tweet_id":"2000351369010807090","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2000351369010807090","title":"@BobScheurle @2ndATexan @DavidCornDC I look at it like this. A: Separate mass shootings (4+) and indiscriminate mass shooting events. B: Faster weapon","summary":"@BobScheurle @2ndATexan @DavidCornDC I look at it like this. A: Separate mass shootings (4+) and indiscriminate mass shooting events. B: Faster weapons that shoot more bullets increased lethality of indiscriminate mass killings, maybe not frequency. C. Gamification of kill counts may have increased frequency","date":"2025-12-14","published":"2025-12-14T23:45:05+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/BobScheurle/status/2000348437326557374","reply_tweet_id":"2000348437326557374","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@BobScheurle @2ndATexan @DavidCornDC I look at it like this.<br><br>A:  Separate mass shootings (4+) and indiscriminate mass shooting events.<br><br>B: Faster weapons that shoot more bullets increased  lethality of indiscriminate mass killings, maybe not frequency.<br><br>C. Gamification of kill counts may have increased frequency</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2000351369010807090","display_date":"December 14, 2025 · 23:45 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
