{"id":"twitter:1998182884419723639","tweet_id":"1998182884419723639","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998182884419723639","title":"Phrase \"subject to the jurisdiction thereof,” based on reading drew on 1866 law and people knew it meant“not subject to any foreign power” and “Indian","summary":"Phrase \"subject to the jurisdiction thereof,” based on reading drew on 1866 law and people knew it meant“not subject to any foreign power” and “Indians not taxed.” Howard never introduced some new exclusions far exceeding tribal sovereignty and diplomatic immunity. Not once","date":"2025-12-09","published":"2025-12-09T00:08:18+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998181579756282040","reply_tweet_id":"1998181579756282040","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Phrase &quot;subject to the jurisdiction thereof,” based on reading drew on 1866 law and people knew it meant“not subject to any foreign power” and “Indians not taxed.” <br><br>Howard never introduced some new exclusions far exceeding  tribal sovereignty and diplomatic immunity.<br><br>Not once</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998182884419723639","display_date":"December 09, 2025 · 00:08 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1998182098998579689","tweet_id":"1998182098998579689","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998182098998579689","title":"If Howard meant to exclude all children born of alien parents why woulnd't he exclude them instead of adding \"every other class of persons?” Swearer p","summary":"If Howard meant to exclude all children born of alien parents why woulnd't he exclude them instead of adding \"every other class of persons?” Swearer presents a novel argument trying to connect two unlinked ideas that have no impact on each other","date":"2025-12-09","published":"2025-12-09T00:05:11+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998181579756282040","reply_tweet_id":"1998181579756282040","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>If Howard meant to exclude all children born of alien parents why woulnd&#x27;t he exclude them instead of adding &quot;every other class of persons?”<br><br>Swearer presents  a novel argument trying to connect two unlinked ideas that have no impact on each other</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998182098998579689","display_date":"December 09, 2025 · 00:05 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1998181579756282040","tweet_id":"1998181579756282040","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998181579756282040","title":"But that is a causual inference that simply does not exist, you can not go from Civil War conscription to read \"partial jurisdiction\" in the debate of","summary":"But that is a causual inference that simply does not exist, you can not go from Civil War conscription to read \"partial jurisdiction\" in the debate of Howard and Trumbull What the Howard quote establishes is excluded categories AND then \"include every other class of persons”","date":"2025-12-09","published":"2025-12-09T00:03:07+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998180934001345014","reply_tweet_id":"1998180934001345014","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>But that is a causual inference that simply does not exist, you can not go from Civil War conscription to read &quot;partial jurisdiction&quot; in the debate of Howard and Trumbull<br><br>What the Howard quote establishes is excluded categories AND then &quot;include every other class of persons”</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998181579756282040","display_date":"December 09, 2025 · 00:03 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1998180934001345014","tweet_id":"1998180934001345014","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998180934001345014","title":"and suggesting \"Given what we’ve just seen about conscription and expatriation, we should read Howard and Trumbull as using a specialized, allegiance-","summary":"and suggesting \"Given what we’ve just seen about conscription and expatriation, we should read Howard and Trumbull as using a specialized, allegiance-based concept of complete political jurisdiction that excludes most foreign parents and their U.S.-born children.”","date":"2025-12-09","published":"2025-12-09T00:00:33+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998180711736717424","reply_tweet_id":"1998180711736717424","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>and suggesting &quot;Given what we’ve just seen about conscription and expatriation, we should read Howard and Trumbull as using a specialized, allegiance-based concept of complete political jurisdiction that excludes most foreign parents and their U.S.-born children.”</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998180934001345014","display_date":"December 09, 2025 · 00:00 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1998180711736717424","tweet_id":"1998180711736717424","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998180711736717424","title":"Swearer goes on to suggest the 14th amendment then “extended birthright citizenship only to the U.S.-born children of citizens or permanent resident a","summary":"Swearer goes on to suggest the 14th amendment then “extended birthright citizenship only to the U.S.-born children of citizens or permanent resident aliens whose consensual integration into American society renders them subject to the nation’s complete political jurisdiction.”","date":"2025-12-08","published":"2025-12-08T23:59:40+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998180379136753715","reply_tweet_id":"1998180379136753715","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Swearer goes on to suggest  the 14th amendment then “extended birthright citizenship only to the U.S.-born children of citizens or permanent resident aliens whose consensual integration into American society renders them subject to the nation’s complete political jurisdiction.”</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998180711736717424","display_date":"December 08, 2025 · 23:59 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1998180379136753715","tweet_id":"1998180379136753715","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998180379136753715","title":"The major thesis of Swearer basically boils down to, “not every person residing within the geographic borders of the United States owed the nation its","summary":"The major thesis of Swearer basically boils down to, “not every person residing within the geographic borders of the United States owed the nation its allegiance, nor was subject to its complete political jurisdiction\" it's used repeatedly in her article","date":"2025-12-08","published":"2025-12-08T23:58:21+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998173799263719625","reply_tweet_id":"1998173799263719625","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>The major thesis of Swearer basically boils down to, <br><br>“not every person residing within the geographic borders of the United States owed the nation its allegiance, nor was subject to its complete political jurisdiction&quot;<br><br>it&#x27;s used repeatedly in her article</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998180379136753715","display_date":"December 08, 2025 · 23:58 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1998173799263719625","tweet_id":"1998173799263719625","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998173799263719625","title":"Swearer is trying to establish that \"partial versus full jurisdiction\" was ever a thing when in reality there is no case law or Congressional debates ","summary":"Swearer is trying to establish that \"partial versus full jurisdiction\" was ever a thing when in reality there is no case law or Congressional debates where \"partial jurisdiction\" was ever established and then uses that to read intent in two different debates.","date":"2025-12-08","published":"2025-12-08T23:32:12+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998173190343004636","reply_tweet_id":"1998173190343004636","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Swearer is trying to establish that &quot;partial versus full jurisdiction&quot; was ever a thing<br><br>when in reality there is no case law or Congressional debates where &quot;partial jurisdiction&quot; was ever established<br><br>and then uses that to read intent in two different debates.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998173799263719625","display_date":"December 08, 2025 · 23:32 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
