{"id":"twitter:1998132573181190347","tweet_id":"1998132573181190347","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998132573181190347","title":"@char5191 @WadeMiller Wong doesn't hold a child born in the U.S. to non-citizen Chinese parents is a citizen? You sure bout that? Plyler v. Doe (1982)","summary":"@char5191 @WadeMiller Wong doesn't hold a child born in the U.S. to non-citizen Chinese parents is a citizen? You sure bout that? Plyler v. Doe (1982) establishes t's a matter of territorial determination If you are in the territory of US, you are subject to the laws","date":"2025-12-08","published":"2025-12-08T20:48:23+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/char5191/status/1998131610156490972","reply_tweet_id":"1998131610156490972","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@char5191 @WadeMiller Wong doesn&#x27;t hold a child born in the U.S. to non-citizen Chinese parents is a citizen?<br><br>You sure bout that?<br><br>Plyler v. Doe (1982) establishes t&#x27;s a matter of territorial determination<br><br>If you are in the territory of US, you are subject to the laws</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998132573181190347","display_date":"December 08, 2025 · 20:48 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1998132057374175642","tweet_id":"1998132057374175642","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998132057374175642","title":"Both Shuck and Smith and Eastman try to use Elks V Wilks to establish a principle of \"mutual consent\" that does not exist in case law Further the Indi","summary":"Both Shuck and Smith and Eastman try to use Elks V Wilks to establish a principle of \"mutual consent\" that does not exist in case law Further the Indian Citizenship Act of 1924 renders most of Elks v Wilks, moot and US v. Wong Kim Ark and Plyler v. Doe (1982) came after","date":"2025-12-08","published":"2025-12-08T20:46:20+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998131189010530517","reply_tweet_id":"1998131189010530517","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Both Shuck and Smith and Eastman try to use Elks V Wilks to establish a principle of &quot;mutual consent&quot; that does not exist in case law<br><br>Further the Indian Citizenship Act of 1924 renders most of Elks v Wilks, moot<br><br>and US  v. Wong Kim Ark and Plyler v. Doe (1982) came after</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998132057374175642","display_date":"December 08, 2025 · 20:46 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:1998131189010530517","tweet_id":"1998131189010530517","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998131189010530517","title":"Elks versus Wilks did not establish a mutual consent decree to naturalization, instead Court ruled members of recognized Indian tribes were a special ","summary":"Elks versus Wilks did not establish a mutual consent decree to naturalization, instead Court ruled members of recognized Indian tribes were a special category, not within the 14th-Amendment Citizenship Clause at birth, because of tribal sovereignty Does not apply to everyone https://x.com/mjsb143/status/1998118307174740200","date":"2025-12-08","published":"2025-12-08T20:42:53+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Elks versus Wilks did not establish a mutual consent decree to naturalization, instead Court ruled members of recognized Indian tribes were a special category, not within the 14th-Amendment Citizenship Clause at birth, because of tribal sovereignty<br><br>Does not apply to everyone <a href=\"https://x.com/mjsb143/status/1998118307174740200\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://x.com/mjsb143/status/1998118307174740200</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998131189010530517","display_date":"December 08, 2025 · 20:42 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
