{"id":"twitter:1998085871858495499","tweet_id":"1998085871858495499","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998085871858495499","title":"@Thelonius_K @WadeMiller I see no reading from 1866-1868 that establishes any concept of mutual-consent relationship. The 14th is written in the posit","summary":"@Thelonius_K @WadeMiller I see no reading from 1866-1868 that establishes any concept of mutual-consent relationship. The 14th is written in the positive rather than restricting with a negative Contrast the 14th Amendment with 1866 Civil Rights Act “not subject to any foreign power.”","date":"2025-12-08","published":"2025-12-08T17:42:49+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/Thelonius_K/status/1998082896134062472","reply_tweet_id":"1998082896134062472","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@Thelonius_K @WadeMiller I see no reading from 1866-1868 that establishes any  concept of mutual-consent relationship. The 14th is written in the positive rather than restricting with a negative<br><br>Contrast the 14th Amendment with 1866 Civil Rights Act  “not subject to any foreign power.”</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998085871858495499","display_date":"December 08, 2025 · 17:42 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
