{"id":"twitter:1998035244432396609","tweet_id":"1998035244432396609","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1998035244432396609","title":"@WadeMiller If you were trying to argue, like Schuck and Smith have, for decades, that the phrase \"jurisdiction thereof\" provides the Legislative bran","summary":"@WadeMiller If you were trying to argue, like Schuck and Smith have, for decades, that the phrase \"jurisdiction thereof\" provides the Legislative branch the right to define birth-right I could entertain that idea, but the idea the 14th amendment can be waived by Executive Order is wrong","date":"2025-12-08","published":"2025-12-08T14:21:38+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/WadeMiller/status/1998032783089021147","reply_tweet_id":"1998032783089021147","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@WadeMiller If you were trying to argue, like Schuck and Smith have, for decades, that the phrase  &quot;jurisdiction thereof&quot; provides the Legislative branch the right to define birth-right<br><br>I could entertain that idea, but the idea the 14th amendment can be waived by Executive Order is wrong</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1998035244432396609","display_date":"December 08, 2025 · 14:21 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
