{"id":"twitter:2072381370496610434","tweet_id":"2072381370496610434","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2072381370496610434","title":"@merill @OniCtwin @techspence MFA, FIDO2, Intune does GPO better (or it's what I know bias), No VPN for remote employees Device configuration, and enr","summary":"@merill @OniCtwin @techspence MFA, FIDO2, Intune does GPO better (or it's what I know bias), No VPN for remote employees Device configuration, and enrollment, device compliance. Way better conditional access. Sychronization sucks, and now identify lives in two places, but benefits beat risk, IMO","date":"2026-07-01","published":"2026-07-01T18:06:36+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2072379853089730630","reply_tweet_id":"2072379853089730630","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@merill @OniCtwin @techspence MFA, FIDO2, Intune does GPO better (or it&#x27;s what I know bias),<br><br>No VPN for remote employees<br><br>Device configuration, and enrollment, device compliance.<br><br>Way better conditional access.<br><br>Sychronization sucks, and now identify lives in two places, but benefits beat risk, IMO</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2072381370496610434","display_date":"July 01, 2026 · 18:06 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:2072379853089730630","tweet_id":"2072379853089730630","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2072379853089730630","title":"@merill @OniCtwin @techspence Just got out of a team meeting on this very topic. I favor hybrid deployment, I think it's lower overhead and convenient","summary":"@merill @OniCtwin @techspence Just got out of a team meeting on this very topic. I favor hybrid deployment, I think it's lower overhead and convenientbut I do work with NIST-SP-800-171 customers. Requirements different For manufacturers, and their MSP, it might be easier than trying to go full AD","date":"2026-07-01","published":"2026-07-01T18:00:34+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/merill/status/2072359378058133623","reply_tweet_id":"2072359378058133623","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@merill @OniCtwin @techspence Just got out of a team meeting on this very topic.<br><br>I favor  hybrid deployment, I think it&#x27;s lower overhead and convenientbut I do  work with NIST-SP-800-171 customers. Requirements different<br><br>For manufacturers, and their MSP, it might be easier than trying to go full AD</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2072379853089730630","display_date":"July 01, 2026 · 18:00 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
