{"id":"twitter:1989723379675304098","tweet_id":"1989723379675304098","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1989723379675304098","title":"@IAMERICAbooted @ZackKorman @merill @techspence As an External Service Provider, Pistachio probably generates in scope Security Protection Data, that ","summary":"@IAMERICAbooted @ZackKorman @merill @techspence As an External Service Provider, Pistachio probably generates in scope Security Protection Data, that resides on their cloud [see 32 CFR § 170.19(c)(2)]. If I could show it doesn't ingest controlled data but just Security Protection Data...maybe there is chance to get the toys https://t.co/ofCiC2vyw7","date":"2025-11-15","published":"2025-11-15T15:53:15+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1989721013194469421","reply_tweet_id":"1989721013194469421","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@IAMERICAbooted @ZackKorman @merill @techspence As an External Service Provider, Pistachio probably generates in scope Security Protection Data,  that resides on their cloud [see 32 CFR § 170.19(c)(2)].<br><br>If I could show it doesn&#x27;t ingest controlled data but just Security Protection Data...maybe there is chance to get the toys <a href=\"https://t.co/ofCiC2vyw7\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://t.co/ofCiC2vyw7</a></p><figure><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"/archive/twitter/media/be4454ad50d13a342eba8f840f4f3672.jpg\" alt=\"Photo attached to archived tweet\"></figure>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1989723379675304098","display_date":"November 15, 2025 · 15:53 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":["/archive/twitter/media/be4454ad50d13a342eba8f840f4f3672.jpg"]}
