{"id":"twitter:1988996554535968937","tweet_id":"1988996554535968937","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1988996554535968937","title":"Naming things is hard. People are troubled with new UX in Teams. It's not just moving features and new buttons. Agnosticaly always disconcerting to us","summary":"Naming things is hard. People are troubled with new UX in Teams. It's not just moving features and new buttons. Agnosticaly always disconcerting to users. You no longer belong to Teams but in Channels. Not a person to the company, but a thing to move through verticals.","date":"2025-11-13","published":"2025-11-13T15:45:07+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Naming things is hard.<br><br>People are troubled with  new UX in Teams.<br><br>It&#x27;s not just moving features and new buttons. Agnosticaly always disconcerting to users. <br><br>You no longer belong to Teams but in Channels.<br><br>Not a person to the company, but a thing to move through verticals.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1988996554535968937","display_date":"November 13, 2025 · 15:45 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
