{"id":"twitter:1988669649005998512","tweet_id":"1988669649005998512","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1988669649005998512","title":"@WazzupDoc7 The invidual mandates would have been nice, not rejecting the Medicare expansion in red states would have helped We would have 50 million ","summary":"@WazzupDoc7 The invidual mandates would have been nice, not rejecting the Medicare expansion in red states would have helped We would have 50 million enrolled That would have brought premium growth down a ton I like private markets. Single Payer system would have the least bureaucracy.","date":"2025-11-12","published":"2025-11-12T18:06:06+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/WazzupDoc7/status/1988669073308414322","reply_tweet_id":"1988669073308414322","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@WazzupDoc7 The invidual mandates would have been nice, not rejecting the Medicare expansion in red states would have helped<br><br>We would have 50 million enrolled<br><br>That would have brought premium growth down a ton<br><br>I like private markets. Single Payer system would have the least bureaucracy.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1988669649005998512","display_date":"November 12, 2025 · 18:06 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
