{"id":"twitter:2070551429496905947","tweet_id":"2070551429496905947","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2070551429496905947","title":"@techspence Realizing I can look at our internal vulnerability and pentesting results to help quantity answer. Who had more vulnerabilities with onpre","summary":"@techspence Realizing I can look at our internal vulnerability and pentesting results to help quantity answer. Who had more vulnerabilities with onprem deployments? I don't think I would bet on the AD only shops beating Hybrid cloud deployments in risk and freq. Gonna play with data.","date":"2026-06-26","published":"2026-06-26T16:55:04+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2070542624860078451","reply_tweet_id":"2070542624860078451","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@techspence Realizing I can look at our internal vulnerability and pentesting results to help quantity answer.<br><br>Who had more vulnerabilities with onprem deployments?  I don&#x27;t think I would bet on the AD only shops beating  Hybrid cloud deployments in risk and freq.<br><br>Gonna play with data.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2070551429496905947","display_date":"June 26, 2026 · 16:55 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:2070542624860078451","tweet_id":"2070542624860078451","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2070542624860078451","title":"@techspence Most of it's just because nobody is going to rip out the onprem ERP and if you need to handle a ton of 3D modeling, more economical to use","summary":"@techspence Most of it's just because nobody is going to rip out the onprem ERP and if you need to handle a ton of 3D modeling, more economical to use local compute, and some EOL on your OT, but 90% it's just PDF viewing. Either onprem AD or hybrid can meet reqs, just debating security","date":"2026-06-26","published":"2026-06-26T16:20:05+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/techspence/status/2070540230117998763","reply_tweet_id":"2070540230117998763","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@techspence Most of it&#x27;s just because nobody is going to rip out the onprem ERP and if you need to handle a ton of 3D modeling, more economical to use local compute, and some EOL on your OT, but 90% it&#x27;s just PDF viewing.<br><br>Either onprem AD or hybrid can meet reqs, just debating security</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2070542624860078451","display_date":"June 26, 2026 · 16:20 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:2070539806401056833","tweet_id":"2070539806401056833","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2070539806401056833","title":"@techspence And I don't hate Sentinel, if you or your MSP know how to us it, super powerful. I just think the learning curve is too much for folks som","summary":"@techspence And I don't hate Sentinel, if you or your MSP know how to us it, super powerful. I just think the learning curve is too much for folks sometimes, and most small businesses I know hate the variables pricing. As soon as you tell them it's a usage rate,folks say nope.","date":"2026-06-26","published":"2026-06-26T16:08:53+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2070539142237196734","reply_tweet_id":"2070539142237196734","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@techspence And I don&#x27;t hate Sentinel, if you or your MSP know how to us it, super powerful.<br><br>I just think the learning curve is too much for folks sometimes, and most small businesses I know hate the variables pricing.<br><br>As soon as you tell them it&#x27;s a usage rate,folks say nope.</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2070539806401056833","display_date":"June 26, 2026 · 16:08 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
{"id":"twitter:2070539142237196734","tweet_id":"2070539142237196734","source":"twitter","type":"replies","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=2070539142237196734","title":"@techspence My vote too.... In the Government space a lot of manufacturers have reasons they can never go fully cloud, I lean on leveraging the AD for","summary":"@techspence My vote too.... In the Government space a lot of manufacturers have reasons they can never go fully cloud, I lean on leveraging the AD for least possible. But it might come down to knowing what your MSP wants, or divorcing them when they can't give you what you need. Lot of…","date":"2026-06-26","published":"2026-06-26T16:06:14+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":"https://twitter.com/techspence/status/2070527788029780472","reply_tweet_id":"2070527788029780472","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>@techspence My vote too....<br><br>In the Government space a lot of manufacturers have reasons they can never go fully cloud, I lean on leveraging the AD for least possible.<br><br>But it might come down to knowing what your MSP wants, or divorcing them when they can&#x27;t give you what you need.<br><br>Lot of…</p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/2070539142237196734","display_date":"June 26, 2026 · 16:06 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
