{"id":"twitter:1983907462542716966","tweet_id":"1983907462542716966","source":"twitter","type":"notes","url":"/archive/twitter/?id=1983907462542716966","title":"Good post from @rodtrent on Classifying Sensitive Data with Purview No built in classification labels for CUI for folks using Purview in 171 environme","summary":"Good post from @rodtrent on Classifying Sensitive Data with Purview No built in classification labels for CUI for folks using Purview in 171 environments. Write the KQL queries right in the eDiscovery tools (formerly content search) https://rodtrent.substack.com/p/classifying-sensitive-data-with-purview?publication_id=1254398&post_id=175832404&isFreemail=tru","date":"2025-10-30","published":"2025-10-30T14:42:52+00:00","author":"Greg McVerry","reply_to":null,"reply_tweet_id":"","tags":[],"body_html":"<p>Good post from @rodtrent on Classifying Sensitive Data with Purview <br><br>No built in classification labels for CUI for folks using Purview in 171 environments. <br><br> Write the KQL queries right in the eDiscovery tools (formerly content search)<br><br><a href=\"https://rodtrent.substack.com/p/classifying-sensitive-data-with-purview?publication_id=1254398&amp;post_id=175832404&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=e5x9t&amp;triedRedirect=true\" rel=\"noreferrer\">https://rodtrent.substack.com/p/classifying-sensitive-data-with-purview?publication_id=1254398&amp;post_id=175832404&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=e5x9t&amp;triedRedirect=true</a></p>","original_url":"https://twitter.com/jgmac1106/status/1983907462542716966","display_date":"October 30, 2025 · 14:42 UTC","access":"PUBLIC","publish_status":"published","is_retweet":false,"photos":[]}
